'''David Benjamin Tomlinson''' {{born|14|August|?}} {{twitter|davbentom/status/1294365424180760576}} is an actor and writer who played several roles (usually aliens in heavy prosthetic makeup), most notably the recurring part of [[Linus]], in {{s|DIS}}, {{s|ST}}, {{s|SNW}}, {{film|14}}, and {{s|SA}}.

Tomlinson's credits include the 2004 sports drama ''Miracle'' (with [[Kenneth Mitchell]] and [[Kenneth Welsh]]) and guest appearances on series such as ''Queer as Folk'', {{wt|Orphan Black}} (starring [[Tatiana Maslany]], with [[Raven Dauda]] and [[Roger Cross]]), ''Conviction'' (with [[Merrin Dungey]]), {{wt|Designated Survivor (TV series)|Designated Survivor}} (with [[Zoe McLellan]], [[Jake Epstein]], [[Chelsea Harris]], [[Etan Muskat]], and [[Vanessa Smythe]]), ''Baroness Von Sketch Show'' (with [[Zarrin Darnell-Martin]] and [[Jamillah Ross]]), ''Grand Army'' (with Raven Dauda), and ''Murdoch Mysteries'' (with [[Clare McConnell]]).

